{"agent_id":"pp3g-N6QB-fact-check-task-per-issue-455-read-it-first-verify","agent_seq":7,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T00:40:50.297899894Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"d4fcea92-4dfa-427f-b7c4-4f338bbd2b96","comment_uuid":"1db5064a-b622-4ed1-af04-e88a0ab033ec","author":"pp3g-N6QB-fact-check-task-per-issue-455-read-it-first-verify","content":"Result: FACT-CHECK of docs/research/deep-research-423-support-systems.md — claim-by-claim verdicts. Method: fork source read directly (/home/claude-code/projects/ASES/fork/opencode-src, matches installed CLI 1.18.13-pp3g-fork; shipped binary grep-confirmed), AgentRM paper fetched in full (arXiv:2603.13110v1), upstream issues #26635/#21728 fetched, official OTel GenAI registry fetched. No edits made to the document.\n\n== TARGET 1: doom_loop (fork 1.18.13-pp3g) ==\n| Claim | Verdict | Evidence | Certainty |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Built-in doom_loop detector exists (doc L17) | VERIFIED | packages/opencode/src/session/processor.ts:372-379 raises permission \"doom_loop\"; agent.ts:121 default rule; string present ×9 in shipped opencode.exe | proven |\n| Triggers after 3 identical tool calls (L32) | VERIFIED (precision caveat) | processor.ts:29 DOOM_LOOP_THRESHOLD=3; :356-366 last-3 tool parts must be same tool + JSON-identical input | proven |\n| threshold=3 hard-coded | VERIFIED | const at processor.ts:29; no config knob (only 3 refs, all processor.ts) | proven |\n| Time window | NONE EXISTS (claim of none confirmed) | logic compares part sequence only, no timestamps | proven |\n| Works per-session (L51) | PARTIAL | window = last 3 tool parts of the CURRENT assistant message only (prompt.ts:1190 creates new msg per loop step; processor reads MessageV2.parts(assistantMessage.id)) → identical calls repeated across separate steps do NOT trigger it | proven |\n| doom_loop will KILL after 3 repeats (L95); auto-terminate loops (L51) | REFUTED as stated | it raises a permission gate (default \"ask\", agent.ts:121); deny fails only that tool call; session/agent is never killed | proven |\n| Configurable as \"doom_loop\": \"deny\"/\"ask\" (L94,L202) | VERIFIED | sdk/js/src/gen/types.gen.ts:1005 (\"ask\"|\"allow\"|\"deny\"); web docs permissions.mdx:164,173 | proven |\n| Upstream v2 surface has doom_loop | VERIFIED | sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts:1681 doom_loop?: PermissionActionConfig | proven |\n\n== TARGET 2: AgentRM paper (arXiv:2603.13110v1, Jianshu She, cs.OS, 2026-03-13) ==\n| Citation \"AgentRM (J. She, 2026)\" (L265) | VERIFIED | arxiv.org/abs/2603.13110 | evidence-based |\n| MLFQ, priority queues interactive vs background, priority boosting anti-starvation (L68) | VERIFIED | §IV-B1: Q0 Interactive/Q1 Sub-agent/Q2 Background; boosting prevents starvation | evidence-based |\n| Zombie reaper: periodic scan, hang >30s, retry or kill (L69) | VERIFIED | §IV-B2: scans every 5s; zombie = lane held >30s while hanging; 50% probabilistic retry; terminate on failure | evidence-based |\n| Token buckets per-API, AIMD backoff, admission control at queue entry (L70) | VERIFIED | §IV-B3 lists exactly these three | evidence-based |\n| DRF fairness across resources (L71) | VERIFIED | §IV-B4 adopts DRF (YARN) over lanes/tokens/memory | evidence-based |\n| Three-tier context active/warm/cold, adaptive compaction, importance/recency compress-not-drop, SQLite+JSONL, 100% key-info retention (L72) | VERIFIED | §IV-C1 Tier0 Active/Tier1 Warm/Tier2 Cold; §IV-C2 value=α·recency+β·importance+γ·key_info_bonus, \"compress don't discard\"; §V-C SQLite=Tier1, JSONL=Tier2; abstract+Tables VI-IX: 99.0-100% retention | evidence-based |\n| Standalone middleware, MIT license (L16) | UNVERIFIABLE (license half likely wrong) | paper states NO license and NO code release; arXiv licenses the paper text CC BY 4.0; doc self-contradicts at L83 (\"likely not available\") | evidence-based (absence searched in full text) |\n| Transparent middleware intercepting API calls (L28) | VERIFIED | §IV-A/§V-A \"transparent proxy that intercepts all agent operations\" | evidence-based |\n| Context manager uses small LLM for summarization (L80) | VERIFIED | §V-C \"Small language model for summary generation and semantic analysis\" (the \"no GPU\" consequence is the doc's own inference, untested) | evidence-based |\n| Research-grade, no turnkey OpenCode integration (L28) | VERIFIED (by absence) | no integration section; §VII-C admits simulated-only evaluation | evidence-based |\n\n== TARGET 3: OpenCode V2 hooks + prompt_async ==\n| V2 session/tool hooks exist (L56) | VERIFIED (capability level) | plugin/src/index.ts:222-335 Hooks: event, chat.message/params/headers, permission.ask, tool.execute.before/after, tool.definition, experimental.*; v2 plugin dir present (PLAN.md/README) | proven (fork source) |\n| Hook into \"shell-exit\", \"read\", \"edit\" (L93) | REFUTED as named | no such hook/event names exist anywhere in plugin API or SDK event catalog (events: session.created/updated/deleted/status/idle/error/diff/compacted). Achievable via generic event hook or tool.execute.after filtered on tool==\"bash\" | proven |\n| prompt_async returns immediately | VERIFIED | fork handlers/session.ts:311-329 forks work into scope, returns NoContent (204) at once; upstream #26635 confirms 204 behaviour. Path nuance: route is /session/:id/prompt_async in both fork source (compression.ts:12) and upstream issue repro — no /api prefix | proven |\n| starts-if-needed semantics | VERIFIED | prompt.ts:1074→loop→run-state.ts:88-94 ensureRunning reuses existing runner or creates one | proven |\n| Regression #26635 (SSE discard, v1.14.44) | VERIFIED | github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/26635: 204 returned, model never invoked, SSE silent; CLOSED | evidence-based |\n| Regression #21728 (agent/model override) | VERIFIED | github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/21728: omitted agent/model silently overridden by defaults via createUserMessage; CLOSED as not planned | evidence-based |\n\n== TARGET 4: OTel GenAI attribute names ==\n| Standardized names incl input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_hits (L34) | PARTIAL | gen_ai.usage.input_tokens + gen_ai.usage.output_tokens EXIST; \"cache_hits\" DOES NOT EXIST — actual: gen_ai.usage.cache_read.input_tokens and gen_ai.usage.cache_creation.input_tokens. All attrs moved to open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai (main registry entries deprecated/moved) | proven (official registry fetched) |\n| OTel gives cache-read tokens (L54) | VERIFIED | gen_ai.usage.cache_read.input_tokens exists | proven |\n\n== CORRECTIONS FOR THE DOCUMENT (comment-only; doc untouched) ==\nC1. doom_loop is a permission GATE (default ask), not an auto-killer. \"Rely on doom_loop\" for auto-terminate (L51/L95/L259) overstates it: even with deny, the agent receives a denial and continues; session termination needs external enforcement.\nC2. doom_loop scope is the current assistant message (one LLM response): 3 identical calls must be consecutive parts within one response. Cross-step repetition (same call every turn) does NOT trigger it — a custom monitor remains necessary, contra L51 \"may not need custom checks\".\nC3. Replace \"hook into shell-exit, read, edit\" (L93) with: generic event hook (session.*, message.part.*) + tool.execute.before/after filtered by tool name.\nC4. Drop or qualify \"MIT license\" for AgentRM (L16): unverifiable; paper text is CC BY 4.0; no code release referenced. Aligns with doc's own L83 doubt.\nC5. Replace \"cache_hits\" (L34) with gen_ai.usage.cache_read.input_tokens / gen_ai.usage.cache_creation.input_tokens; note the conventions moved to the dedicated GenAI semconv repo.\nC6. Minor: prompt_async path is /session/:id/prompt_async (no /api prefix) in fork 1.18.13 source and upstream repros.\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: (a) did not execute the binary to observe a live doom_loop trigger — verdicts from source + shipped-binary string presence; (b) AgentRM numbers taken from the paper's own simulated evaluation, not reproduced; (c) upstream issues read at face value (both closed; fix status of #21728 = won't-fix per label, #26635 closed without visible linked PR in fetched view); (d) Crosslink-side claims in the doc (TUI heartbeat, kill/pause/resume CLI) were OUT OF SCOPE per tasking targets [1]-[4] and remain unverified. Certainties: fork-source items = proven (source read); paper/issue/registry items = evidence-based (primary sources fetched 2026-08-25).","created_at":"2026-08-25T00:40:50.288456707Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:7iAJ8lL5mXdPi15aE2jVSEa6gAMRkJI4DP1FV2xaxvs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgZODhADZsg1JfsxPWxMjPPpOkasQrfosfMLYakhIuxV4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAkPLqiBS0oyIS+xtyAQlOUh29hAVaqcSLFaDyeICK8MKCqIvUa4BobQB0l6o/3/xSaGS1eNG3WrHjT2XJMIVYBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:7iAJ8lL5mXdPi15aE2jVSEa6gAMRkJI4DP1FV2xaxvs","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgZODhADZsg1JfsxPWxMjPPpOkasQrfosfMLYakhIuxV4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCXHcfhvcAQ0RoDTtP9H4lagvIjWjuKJmGJy5WryeHHP+hJ4dmB9Qt8eFBPOh7mPS830o3qaVJ0dADJ7LJO53ws="}
